<title>USA: National Energy Group Q1 net increases.</title>
<headline>National Energy Group Q1 net increases.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months ended</p>
<p>								March 31,</p>
<p>							  1996	    1997</p>
<p> Total revenue				    $3,848	 $13,353</p>
<p> Net income					    432	   1,404</p>
<p> Cash flow from operations		    $2,129	  $7,207</p>
<p> Per share data: Net income		    $0.02	   $0.03</p>
<p> Cash flow from operations		     $0.12	   $0.15</p>
<p> Weighted average shares - primary eps    12,043	  43,967</p>
<p> Weighted average tharce - cash flow	17,120	  49,044</p>
<p>				(in thousands except per share data)</p>
<p>NOTE:  National Energy Group Inc said its weighted average common and common equalivalent shares outstanding include the assumed conversion of the Series B and Series C as if they are dilutive for cash flow.  The conversion is dilutive for cash flow purposes but anti-dilutive for primary earnings per share.</p>
</text>
